# Stochastic Weather Generators: Weather State Preprocessing

This repository contains the data preprocessing and weather state generation 
script for the paper: **"Stochastic weather generators for high-frequency wind vector time series"**.

## About the Project

In high-frequency meteorological modeling, accurately capturing periods of 
extreme volatility (e.g., thunderstorms, fast-moving fronts) is a major challenge. 
To improve the performance of our deep generative model (Time VQ-VAE) for wind vectors, 
we condition the generator on discrete weather states. 

This script processes raw, minute-by-minute surface meteorological (MET) data 
from the ARM facility in Lamont, Oklahoma. It handles missing data imputation 
via Kalman Filtering and classifies each 10-minute time block into a 
discrete $2^4$ factorial weather state based on barometric pressure and precipitation.
